 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Infinitive with zu",
     "texto": [
      "It is used after many verbs and expressions: **Ich versuche, früher aufzustehen** (I'm trying to get up earlier). **Es ist wichtig, Deutsch zu lernen** (it's important to learn German). With expressions like «es ist schwer» (it's difficult), «es ist einfach» (it's easy) or «es ist möglich» (it's possible), **zu** also goes in.",
      "With separable verbs, the **zu** goes in the middle: **aufzustehen** (to get up), **anzurufen** (to call on the phone)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Without zu",
     "texto": [
      "Some verbs go without **zu**: **können**, **müssen**, **wollen**, **sollen**, **dürfen**, **werden** and **lassen**: **Ich kann Deutsch lesen** (I can read German). With «gehen» **zu** is not used: **Ich gehe einkaufen** (I'm going shopping). Watch out: **zu** in front of an infinitive does not mean the directional \"to\" of movement, but intention."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
